    <!-- about -->
    <string name="about_title">About the numbers</string>
    <string name="about_body">Gases are measured at 15 °C and 1 atmosphere, as in the reference work, so 1 kg of CO₂ is 0.53 m³. Every question keeps one volume; the size of the ball or cube is worked out from it. Your error is in volume, not in width: a ball 26%% wider holds twice as much.</string>
    <string name="about_credit">Inspired by Real World Visuals, who drew CO₂ emissions as life-size blue bubbles.</string>
